  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#15w2iD6r",
      "title": "Two threads, two jobs",
      "narrative": "Each tab session has its own coordinator, a separate thread with its own model and settings, started with the tab's first message or Talk. It works in a directory of its own that holds no vault, so it names a checkout with -C on every command. It is the voice model's subconscious: it reads the boards, follows the workhorses and decides what the voice model says. It answers, investigates a little, and hands anything sustained to the workhorse of the checkout it names, which goes on working while it talks. Two tabs can talk at the same time, each to its own coordinator.",
