    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/qKGcB6vZ#9Q8uVxC0",
      "title": "Nobody is told without a listener",
      "narrative": "With no voice session the coordinator never runs, so no news is sent and tell_coordinator answers that nobody is listening. While an unattended session holds the voice the outcome report sends nothing, because nobody listens live: in Archboard that is a recording, and whatever the coordinator answered would be spoken into the video. A context change reaches the coordinator and the voice only as the host words it: Archboard tells the voice what changed on a board on screen, and the coordinator only what an agent outside the session did.",
